# Every environment variable saRNA Designer reads. Copy to .env and edit.
#
# Each one is optional: the package works with none of them set. A test asserts that this file
# and the code name the same set of variables, so a variable documented here but read nowhere
# fails the suite, and so does the reverse.

# --- Courtesy and caching ------------------------------------------------------------------

# An address Ensembl can use to reach you about request patterns, sent in the User-Agent header.
# Ensembl's usage guidance asks clients to identify themselves so heavy use can be discussed
# rather than simply blocked. Left unset, the header still names the tool and its purpose.
# The placeholder below is treated as unset, so copying this file unedited sends nothing.
SARNA_CONTACT_EMAIL=you@example.org

# Root for cached Ensembl responses, one subdirectory per source. A cached response makes the
# cost of a promoter lookup a one-off rather than per run.
# On WSL keep this on the Linux filesystem, not /mnt/c, or file access dominates the runtime.
SARNA_CACHE_DIR=.cache

# Set to 1 to refuse every external lookup and serve only what is already cached. A run that
# reaches for something uncached then fails loudly rather than reaching the network, which is
# what makes a recorded run reproducible. Sequence-only design never needed the network anyway.
# Accepts 1/true/yes/on and 0/false/no/off; anything else is refused rather than guessed.
SARNA_OFFLINE=0

# --- Extending the registries --------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Each of these takes either a single .toml file or a directory of them. Shipped entries load
# first and ids must be unique, so your files add to the registry and never silently replace a
# shipped entry. The shipped files document their own formats:
#   src/sarna/genome/data/promoter_anchors.toml
#   src/sarna/regulatory/data/cell_lines.toml

# Extra promoter anchors: regions to design against, each with its reference point, the kind of
# evidence that point rests on, and a citation. This is how a promoter mapped in a paper but
# absent from Ensembl becomes a first-class design target.
# SARNA_ANCHORS=./my_anchors.toml

# Extra cell lines, each declaring what evidence exists along three axes, expression, chromatin
# and TF occupancy. "available = false" is a first-class answer: an empty panel must read as
# "nobody looked", never as "nothing is there".
# SARNA_CELL_LINES=./my_cell_lines.toml

# Directory holding the AF22 histone bigWigs (GSE108506, about 850 MB, not shipped). Their
# absence is normal and never stops a design run; the chromatin panel reports unavailable.
# SARNA_AF22_DIR=~/af22_data

# NCBI BLAST asks API clients to identify a contact email. Sent only to NCBI when screening.
# SARNA_NCBI_EMAIL=researcher@example.org
